body:
Agent chat endpoint (`/api/v1/ai/agents/:agentName/chat`) rejects Vercel AI SDK v6 messages that use `parts` arrays instead of `content` strings, returning 400 `"message.content must be a string"`. The general chat route already handles this; the agent route was never updated.

### Changes

- **Extract `message-utils.ts`** — Moves `normalizeMessage()` and content validation logic into a shared module, eliminating duplication between `ai-routes.ts` and `agent-routes.ts`
- **Update `validateAgentMessage`** — Delegates content/parts validation to shared `validateMessageContent()`, accepting `parts` arrays, string `content`, and array `content`
- **Normalize before AI call** — Agent handler now runs `normalizeMessage()` on raw messages (extracts text from `parts` → `content` string) before passing to `chatWithTools()`
- **Refactor `ai-routes.ts`** — `validateMessage` and the chat handler now import from the shared module instead of inlining the same logic

```typescript
// Before: only string content accepted
if (typeof msg.content !== 'string') {
  return 'message.content must be a string';
}

// After: delegates to shared validator (parts, string, array all accepted)
const allowEmpty = msg.role === 'assistant';
return validateMessageContent(msg, { allowEmptyContent: allowEmpty });
```

### Tests

4 new test cases covering: v6 `parts`-only messages, mixed `parts`/`content` conversations, assistant messages with `parts` and no `content`, and rejection of messages with neither.
